CMEPS mediator restart I/O: drop the per-FieldBundle collective flush, and
make the duplicate coordinate copies optional.

Tested against access-nri/cmeps at tag cmeps1.1.35-x (17ddb2ee). Two
independent changes to the mediator write path:

 1. med_io_write_FB ended its data pass with pio_syncfile, once per
    FieldBundle. Under pio_typename = netcdf4p that is a collective
    H5Fflush on a file still growing toward 25 GB, ~14 times per restart,
    and med_io_close already flushes on close. Removed. The neighbouring
    pio_freedecomp is kept -- the decomposition is still built per call,
    so it must still be released per call.

 2. Every FieldBundle wrote its own <pre>_lon / <pre>_lat full-mesh
    doubles -- identical for every bundle sharing a mesh, 3.55 GB of a
    25.26 GB restart file at 8 km. (The source carried the comment
    "why is this being done each time?".) med_io_write_FB gains an
    optional write_coords argument, defaulting to .true. so history
    output is unchanged; the restart path passes the new module variable
    write_restart_coords.

Change 1 takes effect as soon as the patch is built. Change 2 does NOT:
write_restart_coords defaults to .true., so the restart file keeps its
historical contents until a run opts out with

    MED_attributes::
        write_restart_coords = .false.
    ::

in nuopc.runconfig. (The mediator reads no Fortran namelist; every
mediator setting arrives as a NUOPC component attribute, so that is where
the control lives. It is read in med_phases_restart_alarm_init with the
same isPresent/isSet pattern as write_restart_at_endofrun, and echoed to
the mediator log beside it.) With it set to .false. the coordinate
variables are neither defined nor written, the ESMF_MeshGet(
ownedElemCoords=...) extraction and its three allocations are skipped,
and the <pre>_lon / <pre>_lat variables disappear from the file -- so a
byte-for-byte restart comparison will differ. Field data is untouched and
nothing reads the coordinates back (med_io_read_FB never references
coordvarnames, and no field carries a CF "coordinates" attribute pointing
at them).

Touches mediator/med_io_mod.F90 and mediator/med_phases_restart_mod.F90.

NOTE: if you edit the Fortran inside this patch by hand, the @@ line counts
must be updated to match, or the patch becomes malformed. Prefer editing a
patched checkout and regenerating with git diff; validate-patch.py in the
delivery directory checks every hunk's counts.

